<</Producer(iText® 5.5.5 ©2000-2014 iText Group NV \(AGPL-version\))/Title(CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE BULLETIN)/Keywords( TOP SECRET\r\n rj+'v\r\n 2002/07/12: CIA-RDP79\r\n 25X1\r\n 0000                                                       14 February 1957     25X'\r\n Copy N0- 131\r\n /    CURRENT\r\n DOCUMENT NO.\r\n NO CHANGE IN CAS i.\r\n INTELLIGENCE                                                          I I DcCLASSIHE=D 25X1\r\n CLASS. CHANCE To: TS s    ~\r\n BULLETIN                                                              NEXT:  1-  JvDAl"f':                                         00\r\n RUTH:  .   70\r\n GAS ' aa*        I EVIE\\NEfi:\r\n OFFICE OF CURRENT INTELLIGENCE\r\n CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE AGENCY        25X1 ,\r\n 00,\r\n TOP SECRET\r\n //'                                      2002/07/12: CIA-RDP79\r\n\f 25X1          Approved For Release 2002/07/12 : CIA-RDP79T00975AO02900510001-3\r\n Approved For Release 2002/07/12 : CIA-RDP79T00975AO02900510001-3\r\n\f 25X1A\r\n Approved For Rew,:leajp 2002/07/12 - CIA-RDP       75,AO02900510001-3\r\n No                                '"\r\n 25X1A\r\n CONTENTS\r\n 25X1A\r\n 25X1A\r\n 25X1A\r\n 25X1A\r\n 25X1A\r\n 3. DANGER OF ANTI-GREEK RIOTS IN TURKEY\r\n \(page 5\).\r\n 25X1A\r\n THE TAIWAN STRAIT\r\n 25X1A\r\n \(page 6\)\r\n 14 Feb 57         Current Intelligence Bulletin         Page 2\r\n Approved For Relea25 A         -   5A002900510001-3\r\n\f 25X1          Approved For Release 2002/07/12 : CIA-RDP79T00975AO02900510001-3\r\n Next 1 Page\(s\) In Document Exempt\r\n Approved For Release 2002/07/12 : CIA-RDP79T00975AO02900510001-3\r\n\f 25X1A\r\n Approved For Meas.                              ,2900510001-3\r\n 3. DANGER OF ANTI-GREEK RIOTS IN TURKEY\r\n ILLEGIB\r\n 25X1A\r\n 25X1\r\n trouble could break at any\r\n because of the Cyprus situation.\r\n recautions are being          25X1\r\n taken to forestall any incident or demonstration which might\r\n result in riots in Ankara, Istanbul, and Izmir.             I 25X1\r\n Comment            There have been numerous indications of\r\n impending communal violence in both Greece\r\n and Turkey, as well as on Cyprus, because of the tension sur-\r\n rounding the Cyprus dispute.\r\n Recent anti-Turkish demonstrations in\r\n Greece were quickly dispersed.  The security forces, which\r\n reportedly have been alerted in both countries, can probably\r\n prevent widespread rioting.\r\n 14 Feb 57         Current Intelligence Bulletin         Page 5\r\n Approved For Release 2002/02allAIA-RDP79T00975A002900510001-3\r\n 25X1\r\n\f 25X1A\r\n Approved For R*7eleas                 -         0975`AyQ02900510001-3\r\n SUMMARY\r\n 9 January - 13 February 1957\r\n THE TAIWAN STRAIT\r\n Report of the IAC Current Intelligence Group\r\n for the Taiwan Strait Problem\r\n 1.  There were no si nifiicant combat o erations in the\r\n area during the period.                       25X1 A\r\n 2.  The first through freight shipment on the Yingtan-\r\n Amoy Railroad reached Amoy in early January, according\r\n to a Chinese Communist broadcast.  The line is scheduled\r\n to be officially opened to traffic after reinforcement of a sec-\r\n tion of the roadbed near Amoy. In the meantime, track-laying\r\n is under way on the Nanping-Foochow spur and ma be com-\r\n pleted before the middle of this year.                       25X1A\r\n 3. Radio Peiping on 7 February denounced the United\r\n States in connection with a press report that guided missile sites\r\n are to be established on Taiwan.  Peiping charged that such sites\r\n would constitute a "bellicose move" against the mainland.\r\n 25X1A\r\n :14 Feb 57         Current Intelligence Bulletin         Page 6\r\n 25X1A\r\n Approved For Release                - 975AO02900510001-3\r\n\f 25X1A\r\n Approved For Release 2002/07/12: CIA-RDP79T00975 002900510001-3\r\n i-v\r\n TAIWAN STRAIT SITUATION\r\n 13 FEBRUARY 1957\r\n GEND.\r\n USABILITY\r\n _\r\n CHINESE COMMUNIST AIRF\r\n IELD LE\r\n _\r\n PRIMARY AIRFIELD\r\n SECONDARY AIRFIELD\r\n AUXILIARY OR EMERGENCY BASES\r\n MIG-15\r\n TU-2,\r\n Z\r\n DESIGNATIONS\r\n CONSIDERED MOST IMPORTANT IN\r\n AREA WITH  PREPARED  RUNWAY\r\n OR FIELDS OF LESSER IMPORTANCE.\r\n RUNWAYS GENERALLY LESS THAN\r\n MIG-17\r\n IL-10\r\n Z\r\n 3\r\n GENERALLY 5000 FEET OR LONGER.\r\n 500 FEET.\r\n LA-9/11\r\n O\r\n o\r\n ILI\r\n ACTIVE BASE FOR MILITARY & CIVILIAN AIR-\r\n CRAFT. SOME BASES USED BY PISTON TYPES\r\n ?         OPERATIONAL        A\r\n TU-4\r\n LI-2\r\n Z\r\n Z\r\n Z t\r\n Z\r\n MAY BE USABLE BY JETS\r\n IL-28\r\n ETC.\r\n -3\r\n INACTIVE BASES CAPABLE OF USE BY AIRCRAFT\r\n ?         SERVICEABLE        -\r\n yk FIELDS\r\n NOT CONSI\r\n DERED C\r\n APABLE\r\n CURRENT STATUS UNDETERMINED\r\n UNKNOWN\r\n OF SUPPORTING SUSTAINED OPER-\r\n ATIONS AT PRESENT.\r\n 118120                                                                                                 t 2\r\n H 0 N A N^~ S\r\n KIANGSU\r\n ~~                 \(                       !\r\n NANKING                               52\r\n HANGHAI\r\n H                           U P   E   H      l~            ~L WUHU\r\n HUAINING  1    ~.J CHIAHSING\r\n HANGCHQWv  CHOUSH~N IS.\r\n I-\r\n o\r\n 3\r\n NING~\r\n JHIU\r\n HINHUA\r\n CHUHSIEN\r\n ~\r\n LUCHIAOOTACHEN\r\n NANCHAN\r\n SHAPJGJAO\r\n 28    CHANGSHA .                                     r ^I                             28\r\n Yingtan_/   ,x  WENCHOW O\r\n ?Juian\r\n 60,000\r\n TROOPS\r\n H NGYANG  ! ti\r\n 0CHIENOU\r\n ~ J'\r\n \(\r\n Looo     Ningte\r\n %\r\n j\r\n FOO~ML\r\n 26         Ir ^.\r\n MATSUS\r\n Yungan NANTAI.?   22,000\r\n H5INCHENG 1\r\n A41\)\r\n 0\r\n TING*     LIEI HENG   I LUNGTIEN\r\n ^ CHAN\r\n ^\r\n G\r\n ~.\r\n 7AOVUAN  TGBHA\r\n s            J'\r\n ? WUCHIU                                                                                          TA\(PEI\r\n _\r\n MAC  TANG HUIAN\r\n ., CHINGYANG                                                                            ILAN\r\n <J     fv~~\r\n ~     \\